<title>USA: Digital loses nearly $6 million in court case - NYT.</title>
<headline>Digital loses nearly $6 million in court case - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three women who hurt their arms, wrists and hands while using keyboards made by Digital Equipment Corp were awarded nearly $6.0 million by a Federal jury in Brooklyn, N.Y., The New York Times reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The verdicts, reached last week following a three-day trial, are the first in which plaintiffs have won significant awards from a computer keyboard maker, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It quoted a Digital spokesman as saying the company will seek to have the verdicts set aside.</p>
</text>
